# Beat: guided walk through bob/logfile against googleapis.desc,
# with the overrides from alice/app.desc already loaded.
#
# Invocation:
#   protolens --descriptor-set $PROTOTEXT_GOOGLEAPIS_SET bob/logfile \
#       --load-overrides alice/overrides \
#       --script beats/googleapis.desc
#
# Re-pin (must print nothing):
#   protolens --descriptor-set $PROTOTEXT_GOOGLEAPIS_SET bob/logfile \
#       --load-overrides alice/overrides \
#       --script beats/googleapis.desc script \
#     | grep 'error:'

title: The logfile, googleapis.desc

steps:
  - text: |
      We reopened bob/logfile — this time against the full googleapis.desc
      descriptor set (25 MB, thousands of types).

      Our earlier overrides are loaded: Entry, Timestamp, rpc,
      SearchTextRequest, SearchTextResponse are already named.

      And now we have heat cues for fields 6 and 7 of the ComputeRoutes
      entry — types that were unknown to alice/app.desc.

      👋 Press space to step.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /3/3
    select_line: true

  - text: |
      Field 6 has a bright heat cue: ComputeRoutesRequest.
      Let's accept it.

      👋 Double-click on the heat cue, then double-click on
         ComputeRoutesRequest.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /3/3
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - type: /3/3 google.maps.routing.v2.ComputeRoutesRequest

  - text: |
      👍 And field 7: ComputeRoutesResponse.

      👋 Double-click on the heat cue, then double-click on
         ComputeRoutesResponse.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /3/4
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - type: /3/4 google.maps.routing.v2.ComputeRoutesResponse

  - text: |
      👍 Both route types are now named.

      Let's look more carefully at the SearchTextRequest.
      Navigate into /1/3/1 — the first (shadowed) occurrence of field 1.

      protolens spotted something there: a bright heat cue for
      google.rpc.Status (score: 8).

      👋 Press `t` to open the type tooltip, then `z` to switch to a
         plain path override, then Enter to commit.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /1/3/1
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - type: /1/3/1 google.rpc.Status

  - text: |
      🚨 That is suspicious.

      field 1 of SearchTextRequest is declared as a singular string
      (the search query). But on the wire it appears twice — the second
      occurrence ("coffee in Grenoble") shadows the first.

      The shadowed first occurrence decodes as a google.rpc.Status
      message — a debug trace injected by the app before the real query.
      It carries Bob's API key in plain text:

        AIzaSyB0b5REKn0tAr3aLk3yD0ntB0th3rTry1t

      Every SearchText call leaks the key to whoever intercepts the wire.

      👋 Press `w` to inspect the raw wire bytes.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /1/3/1
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - annotations: false

  - text: |
      The wire bytes confirm it: the shadowed Status blob is present on
      the wire, before the legitimate query string.

      This is a backdoor, not a bug. 😠

      👋 Press `w` again to return to annotations, then press space to
         continue.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /1/3/1
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - annotations: true

  - text: |
      Let's save our findings and export the full logfile as prototext.

      👋 Press Enter to export.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /
    command: xp alice/logfile.all.node.pb
    advance_when:
      - file_exists: alice/logfile.all.node.pb

  - text: |
      Now press Enter to quit.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /
    command: quit
